Z||000000||JetroGT||09-26-1999||05:49 AM||||<BR>I just woke up. <BR>Saturday morning while driving home from work I stoped to get gas. When I got back to my Fiero and tried to start it, no go. It was about 4:45 in the morning and about 20 miles from home. To make things worse I was driving a coworker home as well. He calls his wife to pick us up at the gas station. After they drop me off I have to wait untill the bank opens up at 8:30. <BR>Now that I have enough cash to retrieve my Fiero I'm off to the gas station in a flat bed. Around 10:30 my Fiero is back in the driveway. The starter is shot. <BR>11:00. I finally have the starter out of the car. While I was under there I found a couple exhaust leaks. Oh well. I wanted that new stainless steel exhaust with the Borla muffler anyway.<BR>Now that I have my core I'm off to the auto parts store. <BR>12:30. I'm ready to install my new starter. No problems. Except for the dirt in my eyes. <BR>When I got done cleaning up it was aobout 3:00. My Fiero starts alot faster with the new starter. I think the old starter was factory. Not bad for a 13+ year starter. That was only 28 hours. The longest I've been up was when I was at a two day ice fishing tournament. After hour 46 I fell off my bucket. I woke up when I hit the ice though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||09-26-1999||04:36 PM||||Well, look at it from the bright side: your car has a new starter and you got to spent the better part of your weekend with your Fiero! I could think of worse things to do on a weekend (for some reason, the words <I>in-law</I> come to mind).||||reg||1
